Unreleased
-------------------

* New optional `DatabaseConfiguration::metadata_jwt_token` (builder:
  `metadata_jwt_token`). When set, it is sent instead of the main credentials
  on the three calls that detect the deployment and pick the load strategy:
  `/_api/version`, `/_admin/support-info` and
  `/_admin/cluster/shardDistribution`. These return metadata only but need
  admin rights, so a caller can pass a token of an identity that has them
  (for example a service identity) and still read all data with the user's
  own credentials. Without it, a non-admin user falls back to the slower AQL
  strategy. Unset or empty: behaviour unchanged. Adding a public field to
  `DatabaseConfiguration` breaks code that builds it as a struct literal;
  the builder is not affected.

0.0.9 (2024-08-29)
-------------------

* RustTLS now being used.

0.0.8 (2024-08-22)
-------------------

* In case a user does not have permission to detect the ArangoDB environment
  related information, like e.g. the shardDistribution, right now we cannot
  detect which data loading strategy to choose from. In this case, we fallback
  to the AQL variant as this always works. Still, if the fallback happens,
  a warning message will be printed. Using the AQL variant will be slower
  compared to the dump strategy variant.
